 0004           ; //  FUNCTION NAME:    MeasureBrgRts
 0004           ; //  DESCRIPTION: Read all bridge voltages and set global ratios Vr/Vf and Vz/Va
 0004           ; //  NOTES:
 0004           ; //    - WORD with wUNITY=1000 can encode ratios from 0.001 to 65.535 
 0004           ; //        which represents impedance from zero via 0.05 to 3276.75 ohms and 
 0004           ; //        VSWR from 1.00:1 via 1.002:1 in 2% steps to ~8000:1 where Vr=3999 and Vf=4000 
 0004           ; //    - 3k ohms can be seen on open circuit at lower frequencies, so we need to 
 0004           ; //      cap the ratio 1000*Vz/Va at WORD_MAX, which is done in wDivide(WORD w1, WORD w2)
 0004           ; //    - Vr can sometimes slightly exceed Vf due to measurement error, but
 0004           ; //      this is capped after correction in CorrectBrgRts and the raw (uncorrected)
 0004           ; //      ratio is only ever seen if verbose pcLink is used in which case assume expert user 
 0004           ; //      and don't hide the measurement errors, but still use wDivide for WORD_MAX safety
 0004           ; //  ARGUMENTS: None
 0004           ; //  RETURNS: Nothing, but sets global variables:
 0004           ; //     g_xBridge.wVzVa (wUNITY x "Vz/Va")
 0004           ; //     g_xBridge.wVrVf (wUNITY x "Vr/Vf")
 0004           ; //-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
